// Title: Macro Enabled In A Potentially Suspicious Document
// Sigma ID: a166f74e-bf44-409d-b9ba-ea4b2dd8b3cd
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-06-21 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: persistence, defense-impairment, T1112
// Description: Detects registry changes to Office trust records where the path is located in a potentially
//   suspicious location
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/inversecos/status/1494174785621819397
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_office_trust_record_susp_location.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\Security\\Trusted Documents\\TrustRecords" and (RegistryKey contains "/AppData/Local/Microsoft/Windows/INetCache/" or RegistryKey contains "/AppData/Local/Temp/" or RegistryKey contains "/PerfLogs/" or RegistryKey contains "C:/Users/Public/" or RegistryKey contains "file:///D:/" or RegistryKey contains "file:///E:/")
